  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On this peninsula famous for its luxury villas, Cros deï Pin is one of the peninsula's biggest beaches, in the heart of the village and very easy to reach. A corner of it is reserved for dogs.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office, the dog-reserved corner is at the far end of the beach, on the left. Dogs must be kept on a leash there but can swim. In July-August, an anti-jellyfish net and lifeguards are set up on the beach.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the coastal path that circles the peninsula is a great walk to extend after the swim; check the local dog rules before setting out.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Villefranche-sur-Mer is a few minutes away, with its Deux Rups beach that the tourist office also cites for dogs.</p>
    </div>

